      "role": "user",
      "content": "We sequenced 96 post-mortem prefrontal cortex samples (about 18,000 genes) across three sequencing runs. I want to split the gene-gene co-expression into the part associated with schizophrenia diagnosis and the part associated with sequencing run. The design table uses the same sample IDs, with 0/1 dummy columns for diagnosis and run."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want to split the gene-gene co-expression into the part associated with schizophrenia diagnosis and the part associated with sequencing run.\" -- available from COBRA.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\nYour question asks for a cohort-level co-expression network. **COBRA** fits that result and scale.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nInput compatibility has not been assessed: your data was not checked against the workflow's required inputs; name your input files to have them checked. This is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
